  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The lines \\(L\\) and \\(K\\) are symmetric to each other with respect to the line \\(y=x.\\) If the equation of line \\(L\\) is \\(y=ax+b\\) with \\(a\\ne0\\) and \\(b\\ne0,\\) then the equation of \\(K\\) is \\(y=\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\frac1a x+b\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-\\frac1a x+b\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(-\\frac1a x-\\frac ba\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac1a x+\\frac ba\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\frac1a x-\\frac ba\\)"
    }
  ],
