    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1981-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Interchanging \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) in \\(y=ax+b\\) gives \\(x=ay+b.\\) Solving, \\[ y=\\frac{x-b}{a}=\\frac1a x-\\frac ba. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Reflection across \\(y=x\\) interchanges the two coordinates",
        "Swap \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) in the original equation, then solve for \\(y\\)"
